pocket-synth
https://github.com/Provable-Games/pocket-synth

This product is a modified version of webaudio-tinysynth by
Tatsuya Shinyagaito (g200kg), https://github.com/g200kg/webaudio-tinysynth,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

Modifications by Provable Games, based on upstream commit
3d75aee4b3f43cbd932265e7d60201fd5b770397:

  - Removed the GUI panel and <webaudio-tinysynth> custom element;
    retained the JavaScript API and CommonJS/AMD/global exports.
  - Preserved fractional BPM from MIDI tempo events instead of rounding
    down; added loopEnd/setLoopEnd() for loop boundaries and
    getPlayStatus().startTime for visual synchronization.
    Explicit loop boundaries preserve the rest before the first event.
  - Added bounded, validated SMF parsing with coded errors that preserve
    the previous song. Bounded sequencer callbacks, stopped non-advancing
    loops and empty songs, and rebuilt tempo/channel state on seek/replay.
  - Added context/destination/lazy constructor options and
    resume()/dispose(). Released voices, nodes and timers; closed only
    synth-owned contexts. Stop, seek and song replacement cancel drums and queued controllers.
    Rejected realtime sequencing on OfflineAudioContext and handled
    resume promise failures.
  - On coarse-pointer (touch) devices, the realtime lookahead (preroll)
    is 1 s.
    The realtime voice limit applies to the sequencer's queued voices
    at their start times, and channel mode messages sent with a future
    time act at that time (CC120 cuts, CC123-127 act as note-offs).
    CC121 also lifts the sustain pedal, releasing the voices it held.
  - Oscillator detune (bend and vibrato) is k-rate, computed once per
    render quantum.
  - Added autoResume (default true) for application-controlled audio
    startup: with false, send() does not resume suspended/interrupted
    contexts and the sequencer waits until its context runs. Explicit
    resume() remains available; suspension retains the song, voices
    and scheduled events.
  - Added argument validation to volume, quality, voice-limit, loop-end
    and channel-message functions, and installed validated timbre copies.
    Legacy setLoop()/setTsMode() assignments remain unchecked. Malformed
    MIDI byte messages are ignored; invalid send() argument types or
    timestamps can throw TypeError/RangeError. Notes with computed
    AudioParam values outside float32 range are skipped; timbre time
    fields are bounded and converted mode-1 timestamps are clamped to
    the current context time.
  - Added cancellable loadMIDIUrl() promises with coded errors and
    protection against stale responses.
  - Corrected note releases during attack to use each operator's reached
    level; retained no-attack operator releases for zero-length notes.
  - Added setSampleWave()/setHarmonicWave() waveform registries and
    optional fixed output-operator filters (fl, ff, fq, fk).
  - Replaced Math.random() reverb/noise generation with independent
    seeded mulberry32 streams; added read-only seed (default 0) and
    bufferVersion. The noise/reverb texture differs from upstream;
    buffer data is repeatable for the same seed, bufferVersion and
    sample rate. Metallic noise is generated once per context
    installation on first use or prewarm(); disabled reverb does not
    generate its impulse. Installed built-in timbres once.
  - Updated demos to use the JavaScript API, user-gesture audio startup,
    error reporting and validated timbre editing. Corrected note/sustain
    cleanup, MIDI input hot-plug handling and competing file/URL loads.
  - Replaced remotely loaded demo controls with a pinned local JavaScript
    copy; removed external custom-element polyfill and Google Fonts
    loads, and unused Polymer controls, sample pages and images.
  - Added locked Node/npm development tooling, ESLint, unit/native Node,
    upstream-regression and Chromium/Firefox/WebKit browser tests,
    deadline-bounded runners, benchmarks and evidence-analysis tools.
  - Added CI, browser-matrix, Codex/Claude review and distribution-rebuild
    workflows and Dependabot configuration. Integration CI regenerates
    distributions after merges; releases on main remain manual.
  - Added pinned, reproducible Terser builds, distribution/inline-safety
    verification, size/checksum reporting and package-install checks;
    regenerated webaudio-tinysynth.min.js and its source map.
  - Renamed the package to pocket-synth; updated its version and
    repository/support metadata;
    replaced .npmignore with an explicit package file allowlist for synth
    source/builds, LICENSE, NOTICE and README (npm also adds package.json).
  - Consolidated maintained documentation into README, NOTICE and AGENTS;
    CLAUDE points to AGENTS.

